# visual regression
# CI (linux) baselines ARE committed — they are the source of truth.
# Locally-generated ones are per-developer scratch and must never be pushed,
# or two machines' font rasterisation ends up arguing in the diff.
visual/__screenshots__/*-win32.png
visual/__screenshots__/*-darwin.png
# CI-only staging for the proposed-baselines artifact.
visual/__proposed__/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/

# The Jetro VS Code extension used to write agent config into every folder it
# opened, overwriting whatever was there. It was uninstalled on 2026-09-13 and
# the files it squatted on are OURS now, and tracked:
#
#   CLAUDE.md          imports AGENTS.md — Claude Code never reads AGENTS.md
#   .mcp.json          XUI's MCP server, for Claude Code
#   .cursor/mcp.json   the same, for Cursor
#   .codex/config.toml the same, for Codex
#
# Jetro's OTHER file names stay ignored, so a machine that still has it cannot
# commit them by accident. If it comes back it will overwrite the four above
# too: CI fails any commit whose copies mention Jetro.
.windsurfrules
AGENT.md
.cursor/rules/agent.mdc
.agents/rules/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
# Everything in .codex/ except the config above — hooks.json there is
# per-machine and has never been shared.
.codex/*
!.codex/config.toml

# ad-hoc debugging screenshots and the throwaway scripts that take them
screenshot.png
shot-*.png
